    {
      "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.25a8ac2d9482b3febf526fddce5088acbb67b98e.001.1",
      "event": "Flood Advisory",
      "severity": "Minor",
      "urgency": "Expected",
      "certainty": "Likely",
      "headline": "Flood Advisory issued October 28 at 4:50AM HST until October 28 at 6:30AM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...The island of Molokai in Maui County...\n\n* WHEN...Until 630 AM HST.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding on roads, poor drainage areas, and in\nstreams. Overflowing poor drainage areas. River or stream flows are\nelevated.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 448 AM HST, Doppler radar shows a large convective band\nproducing heavy rain across the island of Molokai this morning.\nRain was falling at a rate of 0.5 to 1 inch per hour. Minor\nflooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly in the advisory\narea.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nthe entire island of Molokai.",
      "instruction": "Rainfall and runoff will also cause hazardous driving conditions due\nto ponding, reduced visibility and poor braking action.\n\nA Flood Watch is also in effect for Maui County through tonight.",
      "areaDesc": "Maui, HI",
      "zones": [],
      "effective": "2026-10-28T04:50:00-10:00",
